# Patterns

## Server Actions
- File: `app/actions/<domain>.ts` · directive: `"use server"` · return: `SubmissionResult<string[]>`
- First line: auth guard — `getRequiredUserId()` / `requireUser()` / `requireAdmin()`
- Parse: `parseWithZod(formData, { schema })` from `@conform-to/zod`
- Always include `userId` in DB `where` clauses
- Delete/redirect actions: return `redirect("/path")` — no `SubmissionResult`
- Admin mutations: call `revalidatePath()` after DB write
- Full template → see `@add-server-action` skill

## Form → Action flow
- `useForm` + `zodResolver` → `toFormData(data)` → call action → `toast` + `router.refresh()`
- Error toast: `toast.error(Object.values(result.error ?? {}).flat()[0] ?? "Something went wrong")`
- Full template → see `@add-component` skill

## Prisma
- Scope all queries: `where: { id, userId }` — ownership check in one query
- Prefer `select` over `include` when only a subset of fields needed
- Multi-step mutations: `prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => { ... })`
- Use `findUniqueOrThrow` when record must exist

## Plan guards
- Feature gate: `if (!PLAN_FEATURES[usage.plan].feature) return <UpgradePrompt />`
- Invoice limit: `if (usage.invoiceLimit !== null && usage.invoicesThisMonth >= usage.invoiceLimit)`
- Always call `getUserUsage(userId)` first — never query `EmailLog` or `Invoice` counts directly

## Email
- Use `dispatchInvoiceEmail()` — handles logging + failure notification
- Check `isEmailLimitOk(usage)` before calling
- In actions: fire-and-forget `.catch(() => {})` · only `await` for explicit reminder sends

## REST route handlers (`app/api/`)
- Use `auth()` from `@/lib/auth` — NOT `requireUser()` (no redirect in route handlers)
- Return `NextResponse.json({ error }, { status })` on failure

## Arrays via FormData
- Client: `JSON.stringify(arr)` · Schema: `z.preprocess((v) => JSON.parse(v as string), z.array(...))`
